// CROWN — a `!E` parameter bound must reach the caller's own parameter
// through a generalized callee in between: `strict`'s parameter is `!E`,
// `mid` hands it a lambda calling `apply0(h)`, and mid's caller hands `h`
// a performing closure. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 7 through the pinned boot (measured
// 2026-09-23). The bound crossing the instantiation edge must land on the
// COPY this use renamed, never on apply0's own declaration.
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn apply0(f) = f()
fn strict(g: () -> Int with !E) with !E = g()
fn mid(h) = strict(() => apply0(h))
handler eh { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = (mid(() => op())) ~> eh
